Task exclusion-408
SQLite schema:
CREATE TABLE accounts_408(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, active INTEGER); CREATE TABLE items_408(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, account_id INTEGER, amount INTEGER, status TEXT); CREATE TABLE blocks_408(account_id INTEGER);
Obligations: Return id, qualifying_count for active accounts that have at least one item, have NO item whose status is NULL or differs from ok, have NO item with NULL amount or amount < 60, and are not blocked. Each block with a non-NULL account_id blocks that account; NULL block entries block nobody. qualifying_count counts all items for each qualifying account. Order by id.
Public example data: {"accounts_408": [[234, 1], [48, 1], [124, 1], [198, 1], [707, 1], [897, 1], [823, 1], [665, 0], [38, 1]], "items_408": [[1, 48, 67, null], [2, 48, 71, "ok"], [3, 124, 71, "bad"], [4, 124, 73, "ok"], [5, 198, null, "ok"], [6, 198, 76, "ok"], [7, 707, 59, "ok"], [8, 707, 77, "ok"], [9, 897, 74, "ok"], [10, 897, 71, "ok"], [11, 823, 78, "ok"], [12, 823, 77, "ok"], [13, 665, 63, "ok"], [14, 665, 72, "ok"], [15, 38, 60, "ok"], [16, 38, 71, "ok"]], "blocks_408": [[null], [897], [897]]}
Write a reusable SQL query valid for all databases satisfying this schema and obligations, not just these example rows.
Optional procedural memory:
SELECT a.id, COUNT(i.id) AS qualifying_count FROM accounts a JOIN items i ON i.account_id = a.id WHERE a.active = 1 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM items bad WHERE bad.account_id = a.id AND (bad.status IS NULL OR bad.status <> 'ok')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM items amt WHERE amt.account_id = a.id AND (amt.amount IS NULL OR amt.amount < ?)) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM blocks b WHERE b.account_id = a.id) GROUP BY a.id ORDER BY a.id;
